Ala\u2083), zwitterionic, in a cubic TIP3P box (\u2248 25 \u00c5, \u2248 500 waters \u2192 \u2248 1,550 atoms), CHARMM36m.\n- **Secondary (generality, optional):** alanine dipeptide with a methylated backbone (e.g., Ace-Ala-NMe, \u2248 700 waters) \u2014 adds a fast methyl-rotation torsion; main analysis stays on primary; secondary is a confirmatory repeat.\n- Reference MD: NPT at 300 K (Langevin thermostat, Nos\u00e9\u2013Hoover barostat), integration dt = 2 fs; 1 ns equilibration discarded; **3 independent replicate runs \u00d7 100 ns each** per system (fresh random velocities; replicates characterize thermal/statistical noise).\n\n## 3. Black-box MDGEN contract (assumptions, not measured)\n- **Input:** coarse trajectory of frames at spacing \u03c4 = k\u00b7dt (Cartesian coordinates + topology), plus conditioning on total length T and output spacing dt. **Output:** full-rate trajectory at spacing dt (or a set of stochastic draws thereof).\n- **Stochasticity handling:** n_draw = **5 independent draws** per condition; all metrics are reported per-draw and as mean \u00b1 SD across draws; ensemble averaging (of trajectories, or of metrics when phase coherence isn't required) is our uncertainty mechanism.\n- Model weights/version are not sourced here; the protocol is architecture-agnostic and applies to any MDGEN instance meeting the contract.\n\n## 4. Data protocol (controlled degradation \u2192 reconstruction \u2192 comparison)\n1. **Generate reference full-rate MD** (per system \u00d7 replicate \u00d7 100 ns) and, **on the fly during the simulation**, compute and store the full-resolution **dihedral time series** at every dt = 2 fs (the evaluation ground truth *y*). Angles: for each residue \u03c6, \u03c8 and side-chain \u03c7\u2099; for the methylated system also the methyl torsion. 1D scalar series are cheap to store; this is what makes full-rate evaluation feasible (the full Cartesian trajectory need not be stored at 2 fs).\n2. **Store Cartesian trajectory** at 0.1 ps (50 fs) spacing for building model inputs (\u2248 2\u00d710\u2076 frames/run; \u00a7 Feasibility).\n3. **Subsampling protocol (deterministic decimation):** k \u2208 {100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} \u2192 \u03c4 \u2208 {0.2, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} ps, giving coarse inputs *y*^k via decimation from the stored frames. Decide by Nyquist: a torsion libration at f \u2248 0.3\u20133 THz (period 0.3\u20133 ps) remains representable for \u03c4 \u2272 0.5 ps and is **missing/aliased** for \u03c4 \u2273 1 ps. k = 100 (\u03c4 = 0.2 ps, Nyquist 2.5 THz) is the intact-limit control; the fast-loss regime starts near k = 250\u2013500. If the measured reference spectra shift the band, adjust k up/down by one step (pre-registered rule, not ad hoc).\n4. **MDGEN forward passes:** (system \u00d7 replicate \u00d7 k \u00d7 n_draw=5) full-rate reconstructions \u0177^k at dt = 2 fs.\n\n## 5. Metrics and pre-registered thresholds\nFully equivalent dihedral series are compared after 2\u03c0-unwrapping; band-pass filtering to the \"fast\" band [1/(10\u03c4), 1/(2dt)] isolates sub-\u03c4 dynamics.\n\n1. **Frequency-domain (primary).** Welch/multitaper PSD of each dihedral series. In the reference *y*, identify dominant fast peaks f* in the band above the subsample Nyquist 1/(2\u03c4). **Recovered** \u21d4 \u0177^k has a peak within **\u00b120% frequency** of f* and **\u2265 50% amplitude** (peak-above-local-background) at every such f*. Report fraction of (residue \u00d7 dihedral) pairs with all peaks recovered.\n2. **Time-domain (temporal recovery).** Pearson r(y, \u0177^k) on the fast band; **success threshold \u0394r \u2265 0.10 over the best baseline** (per-dihedral). Also phase-aware RMSE after optimal lag alignment.\n3. **Distributional (statistical recovery).** KL divergence of dihedral histograms (48 bins) vs reference; rotamer transition rate (ns\u207b\u00b9) error (\u03c6, \u03c8 and \u03c7\u2081 rotamer definitions) vs reference.\n4. **Timescale.** Autocorrelation decay time of each torsion in reference vs reconstruction (within \u00b150%).\n5. **Stochasticity report.** Mean \u00b1 SD across n_draw for every metric.\n\n## 6. Baselines and controls (the scientific backbone)\n- **B1** linear interpolation of dihedrals at dt (or Cartesian\u2192dihedral; equivalent here).\n- **B2** nearest-neighbor / hold-last coarse value.\n- **B3** cubic spline on dihedrals.\n  \u2192 B1\u2013B3 are structurally incapable of inventing sub-\u03c4 oscillation; they define the bar MDGEN must clear (\u0394r \u2265 0.10).\n- **C1 re-subsampling consistency (model sanity):** coarse(\u0177^k) must reproduce the conditioning input within tolerance (e.g., mean coordinate RMSD < 0.1 \u00c5); failure \u21d2 model ignored the input \u21d2 invalid for this task, mark condition FAILED.\n- **C2 slow sanity control:** a slow observable that survives subsampling (end-to-end distance; \u03c6/\u03c8 rotamer autocorrelation) must be recovered by MDGEN; if MDGEN fails here too, failure is global (model not useful for trajectories at all), not specific to fast dynamics.\n- **C3 shuffled-input control:** randomly permute coarse frames and feed to MDGEN; reconstructed fast-band fidelity must drop to baseline level, proving output depends on the actual conditioning signal, not just prior/self-generated dynamics.\n- **C4 intact-limit control:** k = 100 (nothing lost) must show near-perfect recovery, validating that the pipeline measures recovery and is not intrinsically noisy.\n\n## 7. Success / failure definitions and k_max\n**Success at (system, k)** \u21d4 all of:\n- primary frequency metric: \u2265 70% of dihedral pairs have all fast peaks recovered (C1 pass);\n- temporal metric: \u0394r \u2265 0.10 vs best baseline on \u2265 80% of dihedrals;\n- C3 passes: shuffled-input fidelity \u2264 baseline level;\n- C2 passes: slow observable recovered.\n\n**Partial success:** distributional metrics (KL, transition rates) recovered within tolerance but \u0394r fails \u21d2 MDGEN achieves **statistical but not temporal** recovery \u2014 a distinct, reportable outcome.\n\n**Failure at (system, k):** any of: fast-peak recovery < 30%; \u0394r < 0.10 margin; C1/C2/C3 violated (model ignores conditioning or fails slow dynamics).\n\n**Maximum recoverable subsampling factor k_max (headline):** the largest k in the tested set with Success (monotonicity assumed but verified; if non-monotonic, report the largest contiguous block). Confidence via bootstrap over (replicate \u00d7 dihedral): report k_max with its bootstrap CI (e.g., k_max with \u2265 95% bootstrap support). The answer sentence: *\"MDGEN recovers missing fast torsion dynamics up to subsampling factor k_max = <value> on the primary system (and <value> on the secondary), beyond which reconstruction degrades to (statistical-only / baseline-level / failure).\"*\n\n## 8. Analysis plan (pipeline)\n1. Extract dihedral series from refs, subsamples, reconstructions (robust 2\u03c0-unwrap; MAD-based outlier rejection).\n2. Per (system, replicate, k, draw, dihedral) compute \u00a75 metrics; aggregate over dihedrals \u2192 per-condition distributions.\n3. Baselines B1\u2013B3 applied to the same coarse inputs; compute \u0394-metrics.\n4. Run controls C1\u2013C4.\n5. Decide Success/Partial/Failure per condition; derive k_max + bootstrap CI; tabulate and plot (PSD overlays, r vs k curves, spectral peak recovery rate vs k).\n6. Pre-register the script before execution; report all numbers including failures (no selective reporting).\n\n## 9. Feasibility (design-level cost estimates; to run on a GPU-capable HPC, not the current sandbox)\n- **MD reference production:** Ala\u2083/TIP3P \u2248 1,550 atoms @ ~10\u201350 ns/day/GPU-node \u2192 3 reps \u00d7 100 ns = 300 ns primary (600 ns incl. secondary) \u2192 ~1\u20133 wall-weeks on one GPU node, parallelizable across replicas/systems to ~1 week on a small cluster. Dominant cost; done once.\n- **Storage:** dihedral scalars on the fly \u2248 10 angles \u00d7 5\u00d710\u2077 samples \u00d7 2 B \u2248 1 GB/run; Cartesian at 0.1 ps \u2248 2\u00d710\u2076 frames \u00d7 1,550 atoms \u00d7 12 B \u2248 37 GB/run (float32; \u2248 0.5 GB compressed). Inputs for k \u2264 1000 are \u2264 5\u201310\u00d710\u2075 frames/run; full-rate reconstruction outputs are the volume driver (\u2248 5\u00d710\u2077 frames/run \u00d7 12 B \u2248 0.6 GB/run if stored; recompute metrics streaming to reduce this).\n- **MDGEN cost:** primary passes = 3 reps \u00d7 5 k-values \u00d7 5 draws = 75 forward passes (+25 for the intact control, folded into k=100); secondary adds +75 \u21d2 150 total. Each pass is a full-rate 40 ns reconstruction over 1,550 atoms \u2014 a few GPU-hours each in typical generative-trajectory models \u21d2 ~1\u20132 weeks on a single GPU, shardable.\n- **Analytics cost:** negligible (numpy/scipy FFT on 5\u00d710\u2077-sample series \u00d7 few hundred conditions; minutes\u2013hours).\n- **Runtime gap note:** the provided sandbox (no GPU, no net, no numpy/mdgen/MDAnalysis) cannot execute this; feasibility statements are the designed target-environment budget, not executed results.\n\n## 10. Threats to validity and mitigations\n- **Torsion 2\u03c0-wrapping/transitions** corrupting PSD/phase \u2192 unwrap + band-limited analysis + outlier rejection.\n- **Aliasing contamination** of the fast band from modes below the coarse Nyquist \u2192 band-pass above actual cutoff and report Nyquist-consistent band only.\n- **MDGEN self-generated dynamics (not conditioning)** \u2192 C3 shuffled control and C1 consistency.\n- **Thermal noise indistinguishable from 'recovered' oscillation** \u2192 replicates give CI; require margin over baselines, not just nonzero correlation.\n- **k_max non-monotonicity** \u2192 report contiguous block rather than assuming monotonicity.\n- **Force-field/timescale artifacts mistaken for physics** \u2192 only ever compare reconstruction to same-force-field reference (never to experiment), so bias cancels.\n\n## 11. Deliverables\nPre-registered analysis script + recorded decisions; per-condition metric tables; PSD overlay and r-vs-k figures; k_max (primary + secondary) with bootstrap CI; final claim statement with success/failure/partial classification and all assumptions visible.", "evidence": "Workspace inspection: /workspace contains only task.json (design-only declaration, references absent track.md); filesystem-wide search found no MDGEN sources, no datasets, no track.md; pip list and imports show mdgen/MDAnalysis/mdtraj/numpy/scipy all absent; network disabled (find/grep and import checks all exit non-zero). This confirms a white-paper task: every concrete parameter is an assumption, fixed by this design. Feasibility figures (frame counts, storage in GB, ns/day throughput, pass counts) are arithmetic from the chosen dt/\u03c4/length/atom numbers, not measured runs.", "assumptions": ["MDGEN is an architecture-agnostic black-box generative model conditioned on a coarse trajectory (+topology, total length T, output spacing dt) that emits a full-rate trajectory; n_draw=5 stochastic draws averaged.", "Ground truth = newly generated full-rate MD (dt=2 fs) with CHARMM36m/TIP3P; the same-force-field reference, not experimental data, is the criterion.", "Primary system trialanine (Ala3, ~1,550 atoms incl. ~500 TIP3P waters), NPT 300 K, 3\u00d7100 ns replicate runs; optional secondary Ace-Ala-NMe (methyl torsion).", "Subsampling factors k \u2208 {100,250,500,1000,2000} (\u03c4=0.2\u20134 ps), chosen so the fast-loss regime (\u03c4\u22731 ps) is covered; k=100 is the intact-limit control.", "Metrics/thresholds pre-registered: fast-spectral peak recovered \u21d4 \u00b120% frequency & \u226550% amplitude; temporal recovery \u21d4 \u0394Pearson \u2265 0.10 over best baseline on \u226580% of dihedrals; fast-peak recovery \u226570% for Success; <30% \u21d2 Failure.", "k_max = largest contiguous k with Success; reported with a bootstrap CI across replicates\u00d7dihedrals.", "Execution target is a GPU-capable HPC; the supplied sandbox (no GPU, no MD/numpy/scipy packages, no network) is insufficient to run this design.", "Feasibility numbers (storage, MD ns/day, # forward passes, wall-time) are planning estimates from arithmetic, not executed measurements.", "Secondary system is confirmatory only; the headline answer is defined on the primary system."], "uncertainties": ["No source pins down which MDGEN version/weights actually satisfy the assumed input/output contract; the design treats it as any matching black-box model.", "Actual dominant fast torsion frequencies and the exact subsampling band in CHARMM36m are only estimated here (\u22480.3\u20133 THz); a pre-registered rule adjusts k by one step if the measured spectrum differs.", "Whether the full-rate reconstruction output (dt=2 fs) must be stored or can be streamed to metrics affects the storage budget (\u2264 ~30 GB vs ~0.6 GB/run).", "Whether a public full-rate MD dataset is acceptable instead of generating reference MD would remove the dominant production-cost term but still requires same-force-field consistency.", "Tolerances (\u00b120% frequency, \u226550% amplitude, \u0394r\u22650.10, \u226570%/80% coverage, <30% failure) are designer pre-registration choices; the researcher may want them loosened/tightened before execution.", "Wall-time estimates for MD and MDGEN passes assume typical GPU throughput for the stated system sizes and are not validated here."]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
